# Keep the image small and never bake secrets/data into it.
#
# Patterns here are relative to the build context and, unlike .gitignore, do
# NOT match in subdirectories unless they start with **/ . The old plain
# `*.db` / `backups/` lines only matched at the top level, so the compose
# volume folder ./data (live DB + 15 backup snapshots, 16 GB on the VPS) was
# copied into every image until a build filled the disk (2026-09-26).
# data/ is the compose volume: it is mounted at runtime, never built in.
data/
**/.venv/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/backups/
**/storm_frames/
**/opsum_images/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-journal
**/*.log
**/config.json
**/.env
**/power_debug.html
**/pager_debug.html
**/opsum_debug_*
**/chromedriver.log
.git/
tests/
pytest.ini
requirements-dev.txt
